{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The launcher loads the application's own config/report.conf regardless of the caller's working directory, and ignores a caller-local file at the same relative path.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests from the application root, /tmp, and a directory containing a conflicting config/report.conf all produced the intended configuration. The conflicting caller file contained region=wrong-caller-directory, while the launcher returned region=west and report=weekly, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-952553df4d8d41a7","cmd-e319e7c28c664e83","cmd-3c70facda427437c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the existing application configuration and business output under /srv/legacy2/working-directory-independent-launch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The app.py and application config hashes match the prepared baseline, the config content remains region=west/report=weekly, and that business output was directly verified before and after the repair and restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-cdf1e0f0bb084d4e","cmd-952553df4d8d41a7","cmd-99a0a02fb6404b4e","cmd-3c70facda427437c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The launcher propagates application errors instead of reporting success.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With the application config temporarily unavailable, app.py raised an IOError and the launcher returned status 1. The config was then restored with its original hash and the launcher again returned healthy output with status 0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99a0a02fb6404b4e"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 7.9 and kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 before and after the change and restart. The installed launcher is a POSIX /bin/sh script using the application's existing Python runtime; no package or platform replacement is shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bc2a23d674fe4f4a","cmd-32fcd37be2ae4a19","cmd-3c70facda427437c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The failed initial installation attempt did not pass its first write due to permission denial and has no evidence of changing state (cmd-5c5fcf5c259c4695). Installing the corrected launcher and removing its temporary source directly implemented the repair (cmd-32fcd37be2ae4a19). Temporarily moving the config was a bounded error-propagation test and it was fully restored (cmd-99a0a02fb6404b4e). The reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol (cmd-850c7980f90e480c). There were no failed services or new listening exposures afterward. The restart protocol was complete: pre-restart boot identity and healthy application state, restart acknowledgement, observed interruption, changed boot identity, and recovered system/application/data state; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5c5fcf5c259c4695","cmd-32fcd37be2ae4a19","cmd-99a0a02fb6404b4e","cmd-e319e7c28c664e83","cmd-850c7980f90e480c","cmd-587e859900784dfe","cmd-c21c35c154ba47cd","cmd-0142cf69b3c24afd","cmd-3c70facda427437c","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The repaired launcher is working-directory independent, ignores caller-relative configuration, preserves the intended configuration and output, propagates application failures, survives restart, and leaves the RHEL release and kernel unchanged. Provider-wide restart evidence for node1 is complete and coherent with the lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks timed out in all lifecycle snapshots, so package health was not independently measured. No package-changing executor command is present, and platform observations remained unchanged."]}
